[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/env/great_hall.gd" id="4_hall"]

; Readability pass (ISSUES.md #15). The far half of the board used to sit
; 2-3 stops under the near half and the checker died through the middle. The
; culprit was mostly FOG: density 0.013 against a near-black fog color blends
; distant stone toward black and crushes the light/dark split with it. Fog
; halved and lifted off black, ambient + exposure raised to keep both back
; ranks legible. Still torchlit and moody — the walls and the empty aisles
; stay dark; it is the BOARD that must read.
